A||||32||danny boy||the walmart tire story||||1||
Z||000000||danny boy||04-22-2001||08:03 PM|||| I finally decided I REALLY need tires. After calling around, I decided to go to walmart because they have the tires I wanted about 25 cheaper than anywhere else.And they're open on sundays. I load up my good GT wheels in the Eclipse and head out. I get there and go in, tell them what I want. "Yes, we have them but we can't sell you two different sizes." What??? Uh, those are stock tire sizes."Sorry, we can't sell them that way." (Me very agitated) "That is what came on the car."  "sorry, can't do it". Ended up only getting fronts. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PFF_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||04-22-2001||08:31 PM||||It's amazing how ignorant some people can be.  I have never heard of a tire place refuse to sell tires.  Maybe you could just buy them and have a different place install them or just visit a different Wal-Mart to get the rears.<P>Good luck. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||04-22-2001||08:40 PM||||OH MY GOD! That just slays me! Maybe you could drive aroud the block and put on a funny hat and sunglasses and ask for the rears with a funny accent. What total maroons!<P>PS, didja let them change your oil? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dave Gunsul||04-22-2001||08:41 PM||||Haha! I had this happen to me only I took in<BR>two tire that I wanted mounted. They did do it though. Funniest part was; i told them that one tire was on the pass. seat and t-other was in the back. I went strolling through the store thinking nothing could go<BR>wrong and then I heard my name over the speaker. I went back and they said: "where's<BR>the other tire"? Me; it's in the back.<BR>them: in back of the seat? Me; no, in the back. Them: you better go out there because<BR>they can't find it. I go in and there stands<BR>3 guys scratching their heads. I open the deck and one of the guys says: Well I'll be<BR>damned.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  These guys didn't know there was<BR>a trunk in the back. :-)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I just shook my head.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||04-22-2001||08:47 PM||||Speaking of Wall-Mart, Sam Robson Walton, chairman of Wall-Mart, is now the richest guy on earth. Apparantly he's worth about $10 billion more than Bill Gates.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000005||WampusCat||04-22-2001||08:48 PM||||Well it's good to know the folks at Walmart are there to protect us from ourselves.  As an aside, I just read today that Sam Walton's oldest son is now richer than Bill Gates and is in fact, the richest man in the world.  S. Robson Walton is now worth some $65 billion.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||gixxer||04-22-2001||08:58 PM||||If you order different sizes from the Tire Rack, it sends up a flag, and a guy calls you to see if you know what you're doing.<BR>It's probably all lawyer driven.  ||||reg||1
Z||000007||AkursedX||04-22-2001||10:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B><P>PS, didja let them change your oil?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I just had a feeling I was going to see something about that in here! LOL  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Galen||04-23-2001||12:03 AM||||Theres nothing wrong with wallyworld oilchanges.<P>Dannyboy, all you had to do was raise enough of a fussbeing as nice as possible. If the guy doesn't wanna do it, tell em to call his manager. They CAN & WILL do two differant sizes.. I've seem do it whilst I worked there.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000009||danny boy||04-23-2001||12:07 AM|||| I was nervous enough letting them mount the tires, no way are they touching any other part of the car.<BR>When I still had my coupe I took it to them for an alignment.I heard them call my name,went back and they had the car high centered on the rack.Backwheels were 3" from touching anything.Somebody left something big under the rack and they got my car hung up on it. That's why I don't take them the car, just the wheels. And I definately buy the warranty so if anything goes wrong its covered.||||reg||1
Z||000010||johnt671||04-23-2001||09:20 AM||||The Wal-mart here is a no go for tires.  I went there for tires fdr my Fiero, saw a set I want at a good price and went to the counter.  By the time they got done the tires were a little more than they would have been at the free mount and balance place but I still wanted them.  They only had two in stock and no idea when they would get two more.  I asked if he could order them and was told he couldn't.  So how can I by these tires Iasked.  Reply was the truck gets here at 10 am and if they are on the truck I could have them.  See ya bye bye said I.  they are also being sued over an oil change because the car (not mine) went nose down from 6 feet in the air while on the lift.<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierohoho||04-23-2001||09:59 AM||||You get what you pay for and the squeaky wheel gets the grease. Thats all I have to say about Wally World.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||04-23-2001||10:22 AM||||I actually had a <I>Good Year</I> shop tell me they couldn't align my Formula because it had different size tires, front to back.<BR>I don't go there any more.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>I think goodyears suck, anyway.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000013||stimpy||04-23-2001||10:43 AM||||Better off Wal-Mart then Pep Boys. I took my car in for a flat repair since they were the only thing open on a Sunday afternoon. 4 hours to fix a flat, and the crank-smokin trailer trash that did the work pilfered my change pocket.  <P>Galen, don't tell me you've never read the "Deal of the Century" thread! That's where I made myself (in)famous. I groove on Wal-Mart. The techs actually ask me about proper oil capacity and only once have I seen them with the front compartment open.(???) Plus you can get a corndog and a Korn cd (edited version) while you wait!||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cliff Pennock||04-23-2001||02:23 PM||||/me likes Wall-Mart.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||stimpy||04-23-2001||02:31 PM||||They got Wal-Mart in The Netherlands? ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Spektyr||04-23-2001||02:37 PM||||Wal Mart rocks... I'm a night owl and I HATE shopping during the day.<P>Not only is that damn pesky sun out, but so is every retard.  Sure, night folk are a little weird, but apparently pedestrians are invincible during daylight hours in a Wal-Mart parking lot.<P>My old junker daily driver (a Pontiac Parisienne) was a 5.0 sans muffler.  I could pull up behind a group of 5 people walking abreast down the parking lot eisle, rev the motor (horn was broken, and wouldn't have been as loud anyway) and they'd just turn and look at me like "What, can't you see we're walking here?"<P>I mean this car was UGLY.  Anyone could tell I could've cared less if I gained five extra dents...<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000017||Alex4mula||04-23-2001||02:51 PM||||I took my Fiero once to a PepBoys to install 4 new tires. It had the spare on because one of the rear was out. When I went there 3 hrs later I see my car with three new tires and the spare. I said, What the hell is that?? I tried to explain the service manager but it wasn't until I got him out to show him that he understood. The mechanic didn't know that the Fiero has a trunk space in the back. The thing is that these dumbass guys don't even ask why someone would buy 3 new tires and leave a spare on... Duhhhh....||||reg||1
Z||000018||DJRice||04-23-2001||09:06 PM||||The last time I went to Wal-Mart to get the oil changed in my Fiero, the girl behind the counter offered to marry me because she thought I had the coolest car around.<BR>Unfortunately, This was <I><B>alot</B></I> of girl. (not that there is anything wrong with that, but its not my style....besides I may not have been able to get her home without my jeep)<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000019||DavidHenshaw||04-24-2001||12:09 AM||||The right rear on my 93 Nissan Sentra SER was almost in shreds(I'm not kidding) so I take it to National Tire and Battery. Tell them to put the left front(a perfectly good tire) on the right rear and put a new tire on the left front. "Sir, your car is ready." Go get the car, shredded right rear still there, new tire on left front, good left front in trash. Go figure.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
Z||000020||AusFiero||04-24-2001||01:48 AM||||LOL theses stories are so funny.<BR>And here I was thinking we had all the idiot mechanics over here. Seems they must have an international mechanics institute where they train the stupid ones willing to work for supermarket wages.||||reg||10
Z||000021||Raydar||04-24-2001||10:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>Better off Wal-Mart then Pep Boys. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I second that! An ex g/f took her IROC to Pep Boys to have the brakes reworked. Half way home she started hearing a grinding noise from the rear. When I took the drum off, the locating link for the parking brake <I>fell out</I>. I put the drum and wheel back on the car and we went back to Pep Boys.<BR>I walked up to the (very busy) counter, and dropped the metal link on the counter from about eye-level. I then asked, rather loudly, if parts fell out of <I>all</I> of their brake jobs. <BR>The look  on the writer's (and all the customers') face was priceless.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000022||FieroHarry||04-24-2001||10:35 AM||||[QUOTE]Originally posted by Raydar:<BR>The last time I went to Manny/Mo/ and Jacks. I told them I wanted 4 new tires.<BR>They replaced my correct sized tires with matching sizes on all fours.<BR>You could hear me all the way across the parking lot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Harry<BR>FOCOSEVA<BR>1985 GT 262K+ "TEMPTATION"||||reg||12
Z||000023||Galen||04-25-2001||02:18 AM||||nose down? I've never known a walmart TLE to use a lift with oil changes. They have a pit.. I aint explaining anymore.<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
