Z||000025||LZeitgeist||04-25-2001||07:34 AM||||I don't let a shop - *ANY* shop - do d*ck to my car. Period. <P>However, since I don't have a tire machine at home, when I need tires, I get them online in the sizes I want, no questions asked... I load up the wheels/old tires and the new tires in my folks' station wagon and take them down to a tire repair shop, and bring them in one pair at a time... I tell them that they're different sized tires/wheels front-to-back, and I'm doing it this way to make sure they don't get mixed up, to save them the time and hassle of redoing them (while being polite and smiling, of course)... "Here's this tire and this wheel, and while you're doing that, I'll go get the next set..."<P>They're nice, I'm nice, they're happy, I'm happy, no problems. <P>After swapping out three clutches in '88 Formulas with hand tools in a carport, I don't know that there's anything left on these cars I wouldn't feel better tackling myself. Not sure about getting an alignment - I'd probably try to find a friend with inside contacts somewhere... there's no way I'd just drop it off at a shop. I'd find *SOME* way to do as much of it myself as possible...||||reg||1
Z||000026||Fiero5||04-25-2001||02:25 PM||||When I was 18, I had a beefed up Plymouth Duster. I went to K-Marts auto center and had new tires put on the Crager rims I had on it. I then had them align it. Keep in mind that this Duster was also jacked up in the back. The guy that aligned it did it to factory specs. I hadn't gotten out of the other end of the large parking lot when all 4 tires started squeeling and you could smell the burning rubber. Not sure what was going on I drove out and tried to head home. Only made it under the over pass and to the next mall a half mile away. I happened to see my Dad in the parking lot and told him what it was doing. Alot of the tread was allready worn off! He checked it out and made alot of grunting noises under ther car. He then got out his tool box and adjusted the camber/caster so it wasn't squeeling anymore and we drove it back to the genius at K-Mart. A new set of tires (at K-Marts expense) and another correctly done alignment and I was OK.<P>My favorite though is the place I currently take all our Fieros for inspection. I have this guy so paranoid about what might happen if he jacks the Fiero up wrong on the lift and damages the car, that he does the whole inspection with a floor jack and a long neck flash light! It's the funniest thing I have ever seen. The inspection doesn't take more than 20 minutes max. Of course they know my Dad pretty well, so they know what good work he does on all our Fieros anyway. But still, I LMAO everytime we have one in for inspection.<P>Oh, oh. My birthday is in May. I have got like 8  Fieros to register and inspect all in one month. Ouch!!<P>Welp, gonna be broke again next month! &gt;sigh&lt;<P>Steve||||reg||9
Z||000027||Galen||04-25-2001||04:19 PM||||Fiero5, kmart uses Penske Auto Centers.. Penske sucks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehe okie enough of my childishniss.. no more in this thread for me<P>------------------<BR>Galen - 1988 Hawaiian Orchid Coupe - <A HREF="http://myfiero.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.spinrpg.com/" TARGET=_blank>Spinrpg.com - Free URL & e-mail Forwarding</A>||||reg||1
Z||000028||TheFiero64||04-26-2001||11:06 AM||||Wal-Marts around here don't have auto centers. They are just a regular store. I love to shop at Wal-Mart. <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Fiero5||04-26-2001||12:42 PM||||Well, that was about 20 years ago when that happened. That K-Mart has long since closed it's auto center. <BR>Gee, I wonder why?<BR>Steve||||reg||1
